    "digdeeper": {
      "type": "zeta-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Description",
            "content": "<h3>The daily feel-good <em>capsule.</em></h3><p>Z-83 is the flagship of the ZETA stack. Three plants — <strong>Zembrin</strong> (a South African succulent), <strong>Amatea Max</strong> (an Amazonian holly tree), and a small dose of <strong>clean caffeine</strong> from organic green coffee beans — packed into the proprietary Focus &amp; Energy Blend.</p><p>Most nootropics hide behind 20-ingredient blends so you can't tell what's actually working. We didn't. Three plants. One capsule. Felt fast.</p><h4>Clinical Applications</h4><ul>\n<li>Supports sharper focus and clearer thinking</li>\n<li>Supports steady, jitter-free energy</li>\n<li>Supports calm mood and reduced edge</li>\n<li>Supports daily cognitive performance</li>\n<li>Supports recovery from mental fatigue</li>\n</ul><p style=\"font-size:11.5px;color:var(--zeta-mid);font-style:italic;margin-top:28px;\">*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ingredients",
            "content": "<h3>What's <em>in it.</em></h3><h4>Supplement Facts</h4><p><strong>Serving size:</strong> 1 vegetarian capsule · <strong>Servings per bottle:</strong> 30</p><p><strong>Focus &amp; Energy Proprietary Blend</strong> — 270 mg</p><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Amatea<sup>®</sup> Max</strong> — organic guayusa leaf extract (<em>Ilex guayusa</em>)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Organic caffeine</strong> — from green coffee bean</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Zembrin<sup>®</sup></strong> — <em>Sceletium tortuosum</em> extract</li>\n</ul><h4>Other Ingredients</h4><p>Hypromellose (vegetarian capsule), organic rice extract blend.</p><h4>Why these forms</h4><p><strong>Amatea Max</strong> is a clinically standardized guayusa extract — not just dried tea leaves. It carries L-theanine analogs and antioxidant polyphenols alongside its natural caffeine.</p><p><strong>Zembrin</strong> is the patented Sceletium extract with multiple human clinical trials behind it (mood, focus, anxiety markers). Generic Sceletium powders don't have this.</p><p><strong>Caffeine</strong> from organic green coffee bean keeps the source clean — no synthetic stimulants, no mycotoxins.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Directions & Precautions",
            "content": "<h3>How to <em>take it.</em></h3><p><strong>Take 1–2 capsules daily, in the morning, with or without food.</strong> Most people feel the lift within 30 minutes. Don't take more than 3 a day.</p><h4>Best Time</h4><p>Morning. Avoid taking after 3pm — even small doses of caffeine can affect sleep for sensitive folks.</p><h4>Pairs Well With</h4><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>ZETA MULTI</strong> — the daily Foundation of vitamins and minerals</li>\n<li>\n<strong>ZETA D+K</strong> — the longevity foundation</li>\n<li>\n<strong>ZETA MINOS</strong> — strength + recovery on workout days</li>\n</ul><h4>Precautions</h4><p>Contains caffeine. If you're sensitive, start with 1 capsule to assess tolerance. Avoid combining with other caffeine sources for your first dose. If pregnant, nursing, under 18, or on medication, consult your healthcare provider before use. Don't exceed 3 capsules in a day.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Research",
            "content": "<h3>The <em>research</em> underneath.</h3><p>A few of the studies behind the two clinically-standardized plants in Z-83. Not a complete bibliography — but the work that shaped the formula.</p><div class=\"ref-featured\"><div class=\"ref-tag\">Key Publication · Amatea Max · 2024</div><div class=\"ref-title\">Acute, dose-response effects of guayusa leaf extract on mood, cognitive and motor-cognitive performance, and blood pressure, heart rate, and ventricular repolarization.</div><div class=\"ref-meta\">Helwig NJ et al. · <em>Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition</em>, Vol. 21, 2024 · DOI: 10.1080/15502783.2024.2379424 · Funded by Applied Food Sciences (makers of Amatea Max)</div></div><h4>Supporting Research</h4><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Reay JL et al.</strong> Mood and cognitive performance effects of an Amazonian Ilex guayusa beverage. <em>Journal of Functional Foods</em>, 2018.</div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Terburg D et al.</strong> Acute effects of Sceletium tortuosum (Zembrin), a dual 5-HT reuptake and PDE4 inhibitor, in the human amygdala. <em>Neuropsychopharmacology</em>, 2013.</div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Chiu S et al.</strong> A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, crossover study of the cognitive effects of Sceletium tortuosum (Zembrin). <em>Neuropsychiatric Disease and Treatment</em>, 2014.</div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Dimpfel W et al.</strong> Zembrin, a patented extract of Sceletium tortuosum: a quantitative EEG study. <em>Journal of Ethnopharmacology</em>, 2017.</div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Wightman EL et al.</strong> Effects of caffeine in low doses on cognitive performance, mood, and thirst. <em>Pharmacology Biochemistry and Behavior</em>, 2014.</div>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
      },
